  "notes": "Figures for the ZVB eCitaro (2 x 125 kW wheel-hub motors, 400 V, NMC 622 battery of 243 kWh nominal, battery mass 2.6 t, maximum charging power 150 kW). tractionPowerKw is the peak 2 x 125 kW (continuous 2 x 60 kW). Seats 31 + 1 as published; total capacity not published by ZVB. Width, entry height (door 1/2: 320 mm), door opening width and turning circle are from the current Mercedes-Benz eCitaro (2 doors / 3 doors) data sheet, which lists the same length (12,135 mm); that sheet's drive (ZF AxTrax 2, 440/360 kW), batteries (444/555/666 kWh NMC, Combo2 plug standard, pantograph or charging rail optional, depot plug-in up to 150 kW preferred) and range (\"up to 600 km\", maker internal test) describe the newer build, not the ZVB buses. Axle positions derived from the data sheet: front overhang 2,805 mm, wheelbase 5,900 mm (rear overhang 3,430 mm). Range and charging time of the ZVB buses not published.",
